{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310716,"nonce":"2s8VGB6War0v0n6JPFO33TnwWy4=","title":"FIXED: StdTypes type addition SIGSEGV'd nue llama. Root cause = class alloc size resolved through punned/cross-context TypeIds -\u003e new ...","message":"Adding ANY type to StdTypes.hx shifted every context-local TypeId. The `new`\nlowering resolved the class allocation size via `class_alloc_sizes`, whose\nWRITE key was the HIR context TypeId and whose READ key was\n`TypeId::from_raw(symbol_id)` — two different id spaces over one map. After a\nshift, Q8Cache's punned key landed on a 4-field class's entry:\n\n    new Q8Cache(...)  allocated 40 bytes  (real layout: header + 13 fields = 112)\n\nThe bump allocator then placed the V-cache Q8Cache at K+0x30 and the owning\nLlamaBlock at K+0x60 — INSIDE K's tail. Each ctor wrote all 13 fields into\nspace later handed to the next object. V's 32-bit `headBytes=68` store landed\nin the low half of K's `scaleF32` POINTER slot -\u003e `0x00007fff_00000044` -\u003e\n`append` -\u003e `haxe_bytes_data_address` SIGSEGV. Every byte of the crash dump was\naccounted for (68 = (64\u003e\u003e5)*34 = Q8 headBytes; 0x7fff = stale pointer high half).\n\n\n`class_alloc_sizes: BTreeMap\u003cSymbolId, u64\u003e` (was TypeId), written with\n`class.symbol_id` in `register_class_metadata`. Resolution order at the `new`\nsite (hir_to_mir.rs ~20141):\n  1. same-context SymbolId\n  2. QUALIFIED NAME via `class_alloc_sizes_by_name`\n  3. AST declared instance-field count (static_sig_index) — this is the stage\n     that actually fires for importer-context `new` today\n  4. argcount last resort (pre-existing)\nREMOVED: the `TypeId::from_raw(symbol)` pun AND a `class_type_to_symbol` hop —\nthat map accumulates TypeId keys ACROSS contexts (seeded at lowering entry) and\nis itself poison. `alloc_size_with_inheritance` parent now via\n`extends_symbol` first. Plumbing (`import_class_alloc_sizes`, MirLoweringResult,\nBLADE restore) all SymbolId-keyed.\n\n**SymbolIds are ALSO per-compilation-context.** Q8Cache was SymbolId 4953 in\nthe NUC census, 4960 in the Mac census, and neither matched its id in its own\nmodule's compile (the SymbolId lookup MISSED and stage=ast resolved it).\nbab87ce0's \"only SymbolIds/names cross modules\" is half wrong:\n**only QUALIFIED NAMES cross compilation contexts.** SymbolId keys are fine\nwithin one lowering context; anything imported must resolve by FQN or from the\nparsed declaration.\n\n- NUC llama: exit 0, `[done] 24 tokens (1.829 tok/s, ttft=12.511s)`, coherent.\n- Mac Qwen2.5-0.5B Q6_K: exit 0, 59.6 tok/s, ttft 0.29s, coherent.\n- Suite 170/170 + new `nue_smoke_llama_chat` end-to-end test.\n- MIR A/B: `const 112u64` at both KVCache.new alloc sites, register-identical\n  to the pre-Single baseline.\n- `Single` is now permanently ON in StdTypes (`|| rayzor`).\n\n- `RAYZOR_ALLOC_DEBUG=1` -\u003e `[alloc-size] class=\u003cfqn\u003e sym=.. type=.. stage=sym|name|ast|argcount size=N`\n- `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR=1` -\u003e full MIR dump; grep the `new` site's `const Nu64`.\n- gdb forensics that cracked it: dump `x/20gx receiver`, decode object headers\n  via FNV (`0x1000_0000 | fnv1a(fqn) \u0026 0x0fffffff`, hir_to_mir.rs:38905) —\n  headers identified the overlapping objects byte-for-byte.\n\n1. **CLOSED 71df54f7.** The by-name map isn't missing — `stage=ast` is simply\n   the correct winner when the class's module hasn't lowered yet. But the AST\n   count was **own fields only** (`index_fields` never read `extends`), so any\n   subclass resolving there under-allocates. Now sums the `extends` chain and\n   returns None if an ancestor is unresolvable (partial count = corruption).\n   Also: an unqualified typedef target was never qualified, so\n   `private typedef __Int64 = ___Int64` could not match `haxe.___Int64`.\n   MEASURED: arity-guess last resort 43 uses → **0** across the suite.\n2. **REFUTED as stated, but found a REAL bug — FIXED 3b1a39f2.** Enum register\n   AND lookup both used the raw id, so they agreed. The actual defect: enum\n   reflection through a **Dynamic** receiver was silently wrong (isOfType\n   false, getEnumName/enumConstructor empty, enumIndex = truncated pointer).\n   TWO causes: (a) three id spaces — RTTI raw, `is` sites FNV, box = static\n   TypeId; now all FNV like classes; (b) the Type API takes a\n   compiler-injected type id that CANNOT exist for a Dynamic receiver → it got\n   0 plus the box pointer as the value. Runtime now recovers both from the box,\n   only when the box id resolves to a registered enum. Test:\n   `test_enum_reflection_dynamic.hx`. **Static receivers always worked, which\n   is what hid it — test reflection through Dynamic explicitly.**\n3. **AUDITED (16 reads) + top risk FIXED 7bdff65b.** The map mixes TWO\n   numerically-overlapping spaces: local writes are `TypeId::from_raw(symbol_id)`\n   puns (tast_to_hir.rs:593), BLADE-restore writes are real TAST TypeIds\n   (compilation.rs:3765). A lookup in one space can hit an entry from the other.\n   FIXED: `collect_inherited_fields` — resolved the parent by feeding the punned\n   `extends` to the real type table, then matched fields on raw id equality;\n   its `field_index` IS the alloc size, so a wrong parent = f9674cd7 again\n   through an untouched read. Now takes `extends_symbol` and verifies each\n   candidate field against `field_class_names` (declaring class NAME).\n   **REST CLOSED a995e302** — every acting read now verifies identity by NAME:\n   - `resolve_field_index_candidates`: symbol-match must agree with the\n     candidate's recorded declaring class, else fall through to the name-based\n     strategy it used to short-circuit.\n   - `try_register_anon_view` / `materialize_class_to_anon`: candidate fields\n     checked against the declaring class before entering a name-keyed map.\n   - the two class-by-name scans → `find_class_type_by_name`: FQN first, bare\n     name accepted ONLY when exactly one class answers to it (was: numerically\n     first entry wins).\n   - interface-impl REGISTRATION stopped emitting symbol-id/+1000 aliases —\n     the registration-side twin of the d9d1ecbf lookup fudge. One class's alias\n     can equal another's real id, granting interfaces it doesn't implement.\n   **DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED:** `lower_field_access_for_class` (~30551) keeps\n   the BARE `struct_name`. Its only consumer is the **C99 emitter**\n   (`codegen/c_backend.rs`, MIR→C99→gcc), which is an ALTERNATIVE/EXPERIMENTAL\n   AOT direction — **not** the main AOT (main = LLVM, `AotCompiler::compile`,\n   gated on the `llvm-backend` feature; the C path exists to skip that dep).\n   That emitter names structs `sanitize_name(typedef.name)` = BARE and skips a\n   second same-named class (`emitted_structs.contains_key → continue`), so\n   same-named classes in different packages collide there by construction.\n   Qualifying the MIR side alone would just miss its bare namespace. LOW\n   PRIORITY: fix inside the C99 emitter (qualify emission + reference together)\n   only if that direction is ever promoted. Nothing on the JIT/LLVM path reads\n   `struct_name`.\n   Helpers now available: `class_qualified_name`, `find_class_type_by_name`,\n   `class_names_match`, plus `field_class_names` (field → declaring class).\n4. **CLOSED d9d1ecbf.** The ±1000 candidate fudge is GONE (renamed\n   `class_implements_interface_id`). Verified dead by removal: suite 172/172 +\n   Qwen end-to-end. Extra candidates could only ever turn a should-fail check\n   into a success — a wrong-type cast.\n\n1. `cmd \u003e file 2\u003e\u00261` then piping through sed/grep HIDES exit 139 — capture\n   `RC=$?` on the bare command line. (Hit again: \"EXIT=0\" was sed's status.)\n2. rsync -a to the NUC preserves mtimes -\u003e cargo may NOT rebuild the compiler\n   crate; \"Finished in 1m50s\" is NOT proof. After rsync:\n   `find compiler/src compiler/haxe-std -type f | xargs touch`, rebuild, and\n   verify by BEHAVIOR (RAYZOR_ALLOC_DEBUG / MIR const), not by build success.\n3. NUC build recipe: `~/build_rayzor.sh` hardcodes `cd ~/rayzor` (NOT\n   rayzor-head). For rayzor-head: LLVM_SYS_211_PREFIX=/usr/lib/llvm-21,\n   stable toolchain, `--features llvm-dynamic` (static needs Polly libs).\n4. `cargo build` REQUIRED after editing compiler/haxe-std (RAYZOR_BUILD_ID).\n5. gdb JIT: pending breakpoints on JIT symbols never resolve — hook\n   `__jit_debug_register_code` and re-create the breakpoint from there.\n   ASLR-off addresses are NOT stable across runs here (threaded load).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_stdtypes_type_addition_breaks_nue` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}